{
  "annotations": {
    "list": []
  },
  "editable": true,
  "fiscalYearStartMonth": 0,
  "graphTooltip": 1,
  "id": null,
  "links": [],
  "panels": [
    {
      "title": "Current incident state",
      "type": "stat",
      "description": "What this shows:\nOne operational state: Normal, Watch, Incident, or Recovering.\n\nWhy you care:\nThis is the first decision point for whether the on-call engineer acts now.\n\nHow to read it:\nCompare SLO burn, latency, errors, dependency health, deploy state, and behavior evidence; behavior-change alone can raise Watch but does not force Incident.\n\nWhat to do next:\nIf the state is Incident, open AI Incident Triage; if it is Watch, inspect the top next-action row.",
      "datasource": {
        "type": "prometheus",
        "uid": "${datasource}"
      },
      "fieldConfig": {
        "defaults": {
          "unit": "short",
          "thresholds": {
            "mode": "absolute",
            "steps": [
              {
                "color": "green",
                "value": null
              },
              {
                "color": "yellow",
                "value": 20
              },
              {
                "color": "orange",
                "value": 50
              },
              {
                "color": "red",
                "value": 75
              }
            ]
          },
          "mappings": [
            {
              "type": "value",
              "options": {
                "0": {
                  "text": "Normal",
                  "color": "green"
                },
                "1": {
                  "text": "Watch",
                  "color": "yellow"
                },
                "2": {
                  "text": "Incident",
                  "color": "red"
                },
                "3": {
                  "text": "Recovering",
                  "color": "blue"
                }
              }
            }
          ]
        },
        "overrides": [
          {
            "matcher": {
              "id": "byRegexp",
              "options": ".*state.*|.*current.*"
            },
            "properties": [
              {
                "id": "mappings",
                "value": [
                  {
                    "type": "value",
                    "options": {
                      "0": {
                        "text": "Normal",
                        "color": "green"
                      },
                      "1": {
                        "text": "Watch",
                        "color": "yellow"
                      },
                      "2": {
                        "text": "Incident",
                        "color": "red"
                      },
                      "3": {
                        "text": "Recovering",
                        "color": "blue"
                      }
                    }
                  }
                ]
              }
            ]
          },
          {
            "matcher": {
              "id": "byRegexp",
              "options": ".*hypothesis.*"
            },
            "properties": [
              {
                "id": "mappings",
                "value": [
                  {
                    "type": "value",
                    "options": {
                      "0": {
                        "text": "normal",
                        "color": "green"
                      },
                      "1": {
                        "text": "infra",
                        "color": "red"
                      },
                      "2": {
                        "text": "capacity",
                        "color": "orange"
                      },
                      "3": {
                        "text": "dependency",
                        "color": "orange"
                      },
                      "4": {
                        "text": "deploy",
                        "color": "yellow"
                      },
                      "5": {
                        "text": "behavior",
                        "color": "yellow"
                      },
                      "6": {
                        "text": "retrieval",
                        "color": "orange"
                      },
                      "7": {
                        "text": "agent",
                        "color": "orange"
                      },
                      "8": {
                        "text": "mixed",
                        "color": "red"
                      },
                      "9": {
                        "text": "recovering",
                        "color": "blue"
                      }
                    }
                  }
                ]
              }
            ]
          },
          {
            "matcher": {
              "id": "byRegexp",
              "options": ".*rollout.*"
            },
            "properties": [
              {
                "id": "mappings",
                "value": [
                  {
                    "type": "value",
                    "options": {
                      "0": {
                        "text": "stable",
                        "color": "green"
                      },
                      "1": {
                        "text": "shadow",
                        "color": "blue"
                      },
                      "2": {
                        "text": "canary",
                        "color": "yellow"
                      },
                      "3": {
                        "text": "paused",
                        "color": "orange"
                      },
                      "4": {
                        "text": "rollback",
                        "color": "red"
                      },
                      "5": {
                        "text": "complete",
                        "color": "green"
                      }
                    }
                  }
                ]
              }
            ]
          },
          {
            "matcher": {
              "id": "byRegexp",
              "options": ".*trust.*"
            },
            "properties": [
              {
                "id": "mappings",
                "value": [
                  {
                    "type": "value",
                    "options": {
                      "0": {
                        "text": "trusted",
                        "color": "green"
                      },
                      "1": {
                        "text": "stale_baseline",
                        "color": "orange"
                      },
                      "2": {
                        "text": "low_volume",
                        "color": "yellow"
                      },
                      "3": {
                        "text": "missing_source",
                        "color": "orange"
                      }
                    }
                  }
                ]
              }
            ]
          }
        ]
      },
      "options": {
        "legend": {
          "displayMode": "list",
          "placement": "bottom"
        }
      },
      "targets": [
        {
          "datasource": {
            "type": "prometheus",
            "uid": "${datasource}"
          },
          "editorMode": "code",
          "expr": "max by (service, environment) (metricchrono_sre_ai_current_state_code{service=~\"$service\",environment=~\"$environment\",model=~\"$model\",model_version=~\"$model_version\",workload=~\"$workload\",stream=~\"$stream\",traffic_role=~\"$traffic_role\"})",
          "legendFormat": "{{service}} current state",
          "refId": "A",
          "instant": true,
          "range": false
        }
      ],
      "gridPos": {
        "h": 6,
        "w": 8,
        "x": 0,
        "y": 0
      }
    },
    {
      "title": "Is this burning error budget?",
      "type": "timeseries",
      "description": "What this shows:\nShort-window and long-window SLO burn plus remaining budget.\n\nWhy you care:\nSREs page on user impact and error-budget risk, not on interesting behavior movement alone.\n\nHow to read it:\nCompare burn against 1x sustainable burn and fast/slow burn thresholds; burn above the fast threshold means page-worthy impact.\n\nWhat to do next:\nOpen the slow or fast burn runbook depending on which threshold is crossed.",
      "datasource": {
        "type": "prometheus",
        "uid": "${datasource}"
      },
      "fieldConfig": {
        "defaults": {
          "unit": "short",
          "thresholds": {
            "mode": "absolute",
            "steps": [
              {
                "color": "green",
                "value": null
              },
              {
                "color": "yellow",
                "value": 1
              },
              {
                "color": "orange",
                "value": 6
              },
              {
                "color": "red",
                "value": 14.4
              }
            ]
          }
        },
        "overrides": []
      },
      "options": {
        "legend": {
          "displayMode": "list",
          "placement": "bottom"
        }
      },
      "targets": [
        {
          "datasource": {
            "type": "prometheus",
            "uid": "${datasource}"
          },
          "editorMode": "code",
          "expr": "metricchrono_sre_ai_slo_burn_rate{service=~\"$service\",environment=~\"$environment\",model=~\"$model\",model_version=~\"$model_version\",workload=~\"$workload\",stream=~\"$stream\",traffic_role=~\"$traffic_role\",window=\"short\"}",
          "legendFormat": "{{traffic_role}} short burn",
          "refId": "A",
          "range": true
        },
        {
          "datasource": {
            "type": "prometheus",
            "uid": "${datasource}"
          },
          "editorMode": "code",
          "expr": "metricchrono_sre_ai_slo_burn_rate{service=~\"$service\",environment=~\"$environment\",model=~\"$model\",model_version=~\"$model_version\",workload=~\"$workload\",stream=~\"$stream\",traffic_role=~\"$traffic_role\",window=\"long\"}",
          "legendFormat": "{{traffic_role}} long burn",
          "refId": "B",
          "range": true
        },
        {
          "datasource": {
            "type": "prometheus",
            "uid": "${datasource}"
          },
          "editorMode": "code",
          "expr": "metricchrono_sre_ai_error_budget_remaining_ratio{service=~\"$service\",environment=~\"$environment\",model=~\"$model\",model_version=~\"$model_version\",workload=~\"$workload\",stream=~\"$stream\",traffic_role=~\"$traffic_role\"}",
          "legendFormat": "{{traffic_role}} remaining budget",
          "refId": "C",
          "range": true
        },
        {
          "datasource": {
            "type": "prometheus",
            "uid": "${datasource}"
          },
          "editorMode": "code",
          "expr": "vector(1)",
          "legendFormat": "1x sustainable burn",
          "refId": "D",
          "range": true
        },
        {
          "datasource": {
            "type": "prometheus",
            "uid": "${datasource}"
          },
          "editorMode": "code",
          "expr": "vector(14.4)",
          "legendFormat": "fast-burn page threshold",
          "refId": "E",
          "range": true
        }
      ],
      "gridPos": {
        "h": 6,
        "w": 16,
        "x": 8,
        "y": 0
      }
    },
    {
      "title": "Traffic and saturation",
      "type": "timeseries",
      "description": "What this shows:\nRequest rate beside in-flight requests, queue depth, concurrency, and token budget usage.\n\nWhy you care:\nThis separates overload or traffic loss from an AI-behavior-only issue.\n\nHow to read it:\nCompare current traffic to the known-good band and saturation to capacity limits; rising traffic plus queue and latency points to capacity.\n\nWhat to do next:\nIf saturation leads latency, use the latency-degraded runbook and inspect capacity controls.",
      "datasource": {
        "type": "prometheus",
        "uid": "${datasource}"
      },
      "fieldConfig": {
        "defaults": {
          "unit": "short",
          "thresholds": {
            "mode": "absolute",
            "steps": [
              {
                "color": "green",
                "value": null
              },
              {
                "color": "yellow",
                "value": 0.6
              },
              {
                "color": "orange",
                "value": 0.8
              },
              {
                "color": "red",
                "value": 0.95
              }
            ]
          }
        },
        "overrides": []
      },
      "options": {
        "legend": {
          "displayMode": "list",
          "placement": "bottom"
        }
      },
      "targets": [
        {
          "datasource": {
            "type": "prometheus",
            "uid": "${datasource}"
          },
          "editorMode": "code",
          "expr": "sum by (service) (rate(metricchrono_sre_ai_requests_total{service=~\"$service\",environment=~\"$environment\",model=~\"$model\",model_version=~\"$model_version\",workload=~\"$workload\",stream=~\"$stream\",traffic_role=~\"$traffic_role\"}[2m]))",
          "legendFormat": "requests/sec",
          "refId": "A",
          "range": true
        },
        {
          "datasource": {
            "type": "prometheus",
            "uid": "${datasource}"
          },
          "editorMode": "code",
          "expr": "metricchrono_sre_ai_inflight_requests{service=~\"$service\",environment=~\"$environment\",model=~\"$model\",model_version=~\"$model_version\",workload=~\"$workload\",stream=~\"$stream\",traffic_role=~\"$traffic_role\"}",
          "legendFormat": "{{traffic_role}} in flight",
          "refId": "B",
          "range": true
        },
        {
          "datasource": {
            "type": "prometheus",
            "uid": "${datasource}"
          },
          "editorMode": "code",
          "expr": "metricchrono_sre_ai_queue_depth{service=~\"$service\",environment=~\"$environment\",model=~\"$model\",model_version=~\"$model_version\",workload=~\"$workload\",stream=~\"$stream\",traffic_role=~\"$traffic_role\"}",
          "legendFormat": "{{traffic_role}} queue",
          "refId": "C",
          "range": true
        },
        {
          "datasource": {
            "type": "prometheus",
            "uid": "${datasource}"
          },
          "editorMode": "code",
          "expr": "metricchrono_sre_ai_concurrency_usage_ratio{service=~\"$service\",environment=~\"$environment\",model=~\"$model\",model_version=~\"$model_version\",workload=~\"$workload\",stream=~\"$stream\",traffic_role=~\"$traffic_role\"}",
          "legendFormat": "{{traffic_role}} concurrency usage",
          "refId": "D",
          "range": true
        },
        {
          "datasource": {
            "type": "prometheus",
            "uid": "${datasource}"
          },
          "editorMode": "code",
          "expr": "metricchrono_sre_ai_token_budget_usage_ratio{service=~\"$service\",environment=~\"$environment\",model=~\"$model\",model_version=~\"$model_version\",workload=~\"$workload\",stream=~\"$stream\",traffic_role=~\"$traffic_role\"}",
          "legendFormat": "{{traffic_role}} token budget usage",
          "refId": "E",
          "range": true
        }
      ],
      "gridPos": {
        "h": 8,
        "w": 12,
        "x": 0,
        "y": 6
      }
    },
    {
      "title": "Latency: successful vs failed requests",
      "type": "timeseries",
      "description": "What this shows:\nSuccessful-request p50, p95, and p99 latency beside failed-request latency.\n\nWhy you care:\nMixing successful and failed latency can hide slow successful requests or fast failures.\n\nHow to read it:\nCompare successful-request latency to the latency SLO and known-good p95/p99 bands; slow failures plus queue growth are worse than fast failures.\n\nWhat to do next:\nIf latency is high, open the triage latency decomposition and latency-degraded runbook.",
      "datasource": {
        "type": "prometheus",
        "uid": "${datasource}"
      },
      "fieldConfig": {
        "defaults": {
          "unit": "s",
          "thresholds": {
            "mode": "absolute",
            "steps": [
              {
                "color": "green",
                "value": null
              },
              {
                "color": "yellow",
                "value": 20
              },
              {
                "color": "orange",
                "value": 50
              },
              {
                "color": "red",
                "value": 75
              }
            ]
          }
        },
        "overrides": []
      },
      "options": {
        "legend": {
          "displayMode": "list",
          "placement": "bottom"
        }
      },
      "targets": [
        {
          "datasource": {
            "type": "prometheus",
            "uid": "${datasource}"
          },
          "editorMode": "code",
          "expr": "histogram_quantile(0.50, sum by (le) (rate(metricchrono_sre_ai_request_duration_seconds_bucket{service=~\"$service\",environment=~\"$environment\",model=~\"$model\",model_version=~\"$model_version\",workload=~\"$workload\",stream=~\"$stream\",traffic_role=~\"$traffic_role\",outcome=\"success\"}[2m])))",
          "legendFormat": "success p50",
          "refId": "A",
          "range": true
        },
        {
          "datasource": {
            "type": "prometheus",
            "uid": "${datasource}"
          },
          "editorMode": "code",
          "expr": "histogram_quantile(0.95, sum by (le) (rate(metricchrono_sre_ai_request_duration_seconds_bucket{service=~\"$service\",environment=~\"$environment\",model=~\"$model\",model_version=~\"$model_version\",workload=~\"$workload\",stream=~\"$stream\",traffic_role=~\"$traffic_role\",outcome=\"success\"}[2m])))",
          "legendFormat": "success p95",
          "refId": "B",
          "range": true
        },
        {
          "datasource": {
            "type": "prometheus",
            "uid": "${datasource}"
          },
          "editorMode": "code",
          "expr": "histogram_quantile(0.99, sum by (le) (rate(metricchrono_sre_ai_request_duration_seconds_bucket{service=~\"$service\",environment=~\"$environment\",model=~\"$model\",model_version=~\"$model_version\",workload=~\"$workload\",stream=~\"$stream\",traffic_role=~\"$traffic_role\",outcome=\"success\"}[2m])))",
          "legendFormat": "success p99",
          "refId": "C",
          "range": true
        },
        {
          "datasource": {
            "type": "prometheus",
            "uid": "${datasource}"
          },
          "editorMode": "code",
          "expr": "histogram_quantile(0.95, sum by (le) (rate(metricchrono_sre_ai_request_duration_seconds_bucket{service=~\"$service\",environment=~\"$environment\",model=~\"$model\",model_version=~\"$model_version\",workload=~\"$workload\",stream=~\"$stream\",traffic_role=~\"$traffic_role\",outcome=\"failed\"}[2m])))",
          "legendFormat": "failed p95",
          "refId": "D",
          "range": true
        },
        {
          "datasource": {
            "type": "prometheus",
            "uid": "${datasource}"
          },
          "editorMode": "code",
          "expr": "vector(1.0)",
          "legendFormat": "latency SLO target",
          "refId": "E",
          "range": true
        }
      ],
      "gridPos": {
        "h": 8,
        "w": 12,
        "x": 12,
        "y": 6
      }
    },
    {
      "title": "What kind of errors are users seeing?",
      "type": "timeseries",
      "description": "What this shows:\nError rate split by application, provider, timeout, rate limit, policy, retrieval, tool, and unknown classes.\n\nWhy you care:\nError class is routing information for the on-call engineer.\n\nHow to read it:\nCompare each class to its normal baseline; provider and rate-limit errors route to dependency investigation, while policy blocks may indicate prompt or input shift.\n\nWhat to do next:\nOpen the error decomposition panel and the matching runbook for the dominant error class.",
      "datasource": {
        "type": "prometheus",
        "uid": "${datasource}"
      },
      "fieldConfig": {
        "defaults": {
          "unit": "ops",
          "thresholds": {
            "mode": "absolute",
            "steps": [
              {
                "color": "green",
                "value": null
              },
              {
                "color": "yellow",
                "value": 20
              },
              {
                "color": "orange",
                "value": 50
              },
              {
                "color": "red",
                "value": 75
              }
            ]
          }
        },
        "overrides": []
      },
      "options": {
        "legend": {
          "displayMode": "list",
          "placement": "bottom"
        }
      },
      "targets": [
        {
          "datasource": {
            "type": "prometheus",
            "uid": "${datasource}"
          },
          "editorMode": "code",
          "expr": "sum by (error_class) (rate(metricchrono_sre_ai_errors_total{service=~\"$service\",environment=~\"$environment\",model=~\"$model\",model_version=~\"$model_version\",workload=~\"$workload\",stream=~\"$stream\",traffic_role=~\"$traffic_role\",error_class=~\".*\"}[2m]))",
          "legendFormat": "{{error_class}}",
          "refId": "A",
          "range": true
        }
      ],
      "gridPos": {
        "h": 8,
        "w": 12,
        "x": 0,
        "y": 14
      }
    },
    {
      "title": "Is AI behavior changing while service health is normal?",
      "type": "timeseries",
      "description": "What this shows:\nBehavior-change score beside error rate, p95 latency, and quality proxy.\n\nWhy you care:\nThis catches silent AI behavior movement when golden signals are green.\n\nHow to read it:\nCompare behavior-change to the normal baseline while checking latency, errors, and quality; behavior rising with normal health routes to AI/model owners, not infrastructure restarts.\n\nWhat to do next:\nOpen AI Incident Triage and use the behavior-changed runbook.",
      "datasource": {
        "type": "prometheus",
        "uid": "${datasource}"
      },
      "fieldConfig": {
        "defaults": {
          "unit": "short",
          "thresholds": {
            "mode": "absolute",
            "steps": [
              {
                "color": "green",
                "value": null
              },
              {
                "color": "yellow",
                "value": 20
              },
              {
                "color": "orange",
                "value": 50
              },
              {
                "color": "red",
                "value": 75
              }
            ]
          }
        },
        "overrides": []
      },
      "options": {
        "legend": {
          "displayMode": "list",
          "placement": "bottom"
        }
      },
      "targets": [
        {
          "datasource": {
            "type": "prometheus",
            "uid": "${datasource}"
          },
          "editorMode": "code",
          "expr": "metricchrono_sre_ai_behavior_change_score{service=~\"$service\",environment=~\"$environment\",model=~\"$model\",model_version=~\"$model_version\",workload=~\"$workload\",stream=~\"$stream\",traffic_role=~\"$traffic_role\",comparison=~\"$comparison\"}",
          "legendFormat": "{{traffic_role}} behavior",
          "refId": "A",
          "range": true
        },
        {
          "datasource": {
            "type": "prometheus",
            "uid": "${datasource}"
          },
          "editorMode": "code",
          "expr": "sum by (service) (rate(metricchrono_sre_ai_errors_total{service=~\"$service\",environment=~\"$environment\",model=~\"$model\",model_version=~\"$model_version\",workload=~\"$workload\",stream=~\"$stream\",traffic_role=~\"$traffic_role\"}[2m]))",
          "legendFormat": "error rate",
          "refId": "B",
          "range": true
        },
        {
          "datasource": {
            "type": "prometheus",
            "uid": "${datasource}"
          },
          "editorMode": "code",
          "expr": "histogram_quantile(0.95, sum by (le) (rate(metricchrono_sre_ai_request_duration_seconds_bucket{service=~\"$service\",environment=~\"$environment\",model=~\"$model\",model_version=~\"$model_version\",workload=~\"$workload\",stream=~\"$stream\",traffic_role=~\"$traffic_role\",outcome=\"success\"}[2m])))",
          "legendFormat": "success p95",
          "refId": "C",
          "range": true
        },
        {
          "datasource": {
            "type": "prometheus",
            "uid": "${datasource}"
          },
          "editorMode": "code",
          "expr": "metricchrono_sre_ai_quality_proxy{service=~\"$service\",environment=~\"$environment\",model=~\"$model\",model_version=~\"$model_version\",workload=~\"$workload\",stream=~\"$stream\",traffic_role=~\"$traffic_role\"}",
          "legendFormat": "{{traffic_role}} quality proxy",
          "refId": "D",
          "range": true
        }
      ],
      "gridPos": {
        "h": 8,
        "w": 12,
        "x": 12,
        "y": 14
      }
    },
    {
      "title": "Did this start after a deploy?",
      "type": "state-timeline",
      "description": "What this shows:\nActive app, model, prompt, index, and config versions for deploy correlation.\n\nWhy you care:\nRecent changes are often the fastest path to mitigation or rollback.\n\nHow to read it:\nCompare before and after deploy windows; if behavior jumps after a version becomes active, inspect rollout, prompt, model, index, or config.\n\nWhat to do next:\nOpen AI Release Guardrail for canary, stable, previous-version, and rollback evidence.",
      "datasource": {
        "type": "prometheus",
        "uid": "${datasource}"
      },
      "fieldConfig": {
        "defaults": {
          "unit": "short",
          "thresholds": {
            "mode": "absolute",
            "steps": [
              {
                "color": "green",
                "value": null
              },
              {
                "color": "yellow",
                "value": 20
              },
              {
                "color": "orange",
                "value": 50
              },
              {
                "color": "red",
                "value": 75
              }
            ]
          }
        },
        "overrides": [
          {
            "matcher": {
              "id": "byRegexp",
              "options": ".*state.*|.*current.*"
            },
            "properties": [
              {
                "id": "mappings",
                "value": [
                  {
                    "type": "value",
                    "options": {
                      "0": {
                        "text": "Normal",
                        "color": "green"
                      },
                      "1": {
                        "text": "Watch",
                        "color": "yellow"
                      },
                      "2": {
                        "text": "Incident",
                        "color": "red"
                      },
                      "3": {
                        "text": "Recovering",
                        "color": "blue"
                      }
                    }
                  }
                ]
              }
            ]
          },
          {
            "matcher": {
              "id": "byRegexp",
